## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide for Next.js:

- **Import:** Uses the Next.js-specific import path: `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
- **Component Placement:** The `<SpeedInsights />` component is placed inside the `<body>` tag of the root layout
- **Framework:** Next.js 16.4.2 with App Router (app directory structure)

## Notes

- The Speed Insights component was already configured in a previous pull request (commit 0b12766)
- No code changes were needed as the implementation was already correct
- The configuration will automatically track performance metrics when deployed to Vercel
- Data will be available in the Vercel dashboard under the "Speed Insights" tab after users visit the site

## Next Steps for Deployment

When deployed to Vercel, Speed Insights will automatically:
1. Inject the tracking script into the application
2. Collect Core Web Vitals metrics (LCP, FID, CLS, etc.)
3. Display performance data in the Vercel dashboard

No additional configuration is required. The implementation is production-ready.
